File List Download:

Synopsis to read the output from GKupload V3.08 and above to create a file
list of all areas that the user has access to.

    The advantage of this over the current system is that the user will
only get a list of areas that you as Sysop gives them access for. Gkupload
will create a file for each area numbered from one to the highest area
number in the BBS:bulletins/ directory area 1 is '1' area 2 is '2' etc and
all this script does is to change to each areanumber in your system and if
the user has access adds this number to a string this string then becomes
the template for the join command which creates a file called 'T:BBSFiles'
this file is then archived using 'C:lha' at which time the user is
presented with a prompt to select the download protocol and then they can
download a full list of files from your BBS.

    Setup is easy just set it up in the files.rx file like you would any
other ARexx script assign an access level and flags and away you go any
problems then let me know. If you wish to have some information about your
System in the full files list place this Information in a file called
'head' in your BBS/Bulletins directory

    
                Cheers Greg!
